=== DOES ALLOWING INDIVIDUAL SENSITIVITY IMPROVE THE FIT? ===
Likelihood-ratio test against the random-intercept model. The p-value is
conservative here, because testing a variance at its lower boundary of zero
makes the standard test too strict: a non-significant result is genuinely
non-significant.

